Notebook[{
Cell[BoxData["Quit"], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.930808220842889*^9, 3.930808221540553*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[121]:=",ExpressionUUID->"404b34b4-1c62-4a4a-ab58-10e46105ec10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The notebook presents the computation of the spin corrections to the \
partial amplitudes and fluxes in the Hamilton-Jacobi formalism. ",
 StyleBox["See PRD 111, 044009",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 StyleBox[" \
(https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevD.111.044009 )",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 "\nSpecifically, it includes:\n- examples on how to use the package ",
 StyleBox["SpinOrbitsHamiltonJacobi",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ",\n- examples on how to use the package ",
 StyleBox["TeukolskySpinFluxesHamiltonJacobi",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\n- comparisons with the results of ",
 StyleBox["Skoup\[YAcute] et at, PRD 108, 044041 \
(https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevD.108.044041 )\n- \
computation of the corrections due spin precession on the asymptotic partial \
amplitudes\n- computation of waveform snapshots\n- some convergence tests of \
the amplitudes and fluxes in terms of the Fourier harmonics modes in the \
orbits  (see the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Convergence tests\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] chapter)",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.929334722204886*^9, 3.929334797609847*^9}, {
   3.929347181619532*^9, 3.929347183118011*^9}, {3.936264332948119*^9, 
   3.9362643636009407`*^9}, {3.93626444420625*^9, 3.936264529717639*^9}, {
   3.936264982317072*^9, 3.936265043585267*^9}, {3.936265086722975*^9, 
   3.936265146510387*^9}, {3.93626547007238*^9, 3.9362655312630777`*^9}, 
   3.936265650428577*^9, {3.936265707401931*^9, 3.9362657093445883`*^9}, {
   3.936265846701242*^9, 3.936265856341382*^9}, {3.937534346958817*^9, 
   3.937534383108329*^9}, {3.969207030953203*^9, 3.9692070751113*^9}, {
   3.969207317381934*^9, 3.969207346598557*^9}},
 FontSize->18,ExpressionUUID->"1fbc8ef1-7537-4c8f-bf09-6efbcbc0d6f1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "PREREQUISITEs: the following packages are needed\n-  ",
 StyleBox["SpinOrbitsHamiltonJacobi",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\n- ",
 StyleBox["SpinOrbitsHamiltonJacobiNoChop",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (see the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Convergence tests\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
chapter)\n- ",
 StyleBox["TeukolskySpinFluxesHamiltonJacobi",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (developed with contributions from the code of ",
 StyleBox["PRD 108, 044041",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 " (",
 StyleBox["https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevD.108.044041 ",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 StyleBox[")",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 "\n- ",
 StyleBox["Teukolsky",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["KerrGeodesics",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " from the BPToolkit. These package are only needed for testing, and are not \
required by ",
 StyleBox["TeukolskySpinFluxesHamiltonJacobi",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\n- a modified version of the ",
 StyleBox["SpinWeightedSpheroidalHarmonics",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " from the BPToolkit ",
 StyleBox["(",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["https://zenodo.org/records/8091168 ",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 ") . The mod was developed in ",
 StyleBox[" PRD 104, 124019 \
(https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevD.104.124019 )",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 "\n  To load it properly, make sure that ",
 StyleBox["mod_SpinWeightedSpheroidalHarmonics2",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " has the same version number or higher compare to the vanilla ",
 StyleBox["SpinWeightedSpheroidalHarmonics",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " package. The version can be checked in PacletInfo.wl contain inside the \
folder \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]mod_SpinWeightedSpheroidalHarmonics2\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. To update the version of the ",
 StyleBox["mod_SpinWeightedSpheroidalHarmonics2",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " , open PacletInfo.wl , increase the number in \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Version\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], then run the command \
PacletDataRebuild[]"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.935979797858018*^9, {3.93597987364237*^9, 3.935979887042235*^9}, {
